{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\": \"submission-c4-history.json\", \"summary\": \"Turn 80 strengthened the crash finding by constructing the history that leads to it, closing the limitation the first artifact carried.\\n\\nWhat changed. The first C4 artifact fixed two messages — a recovery-led PreAccept and a legal NOOP Commit — and the review recorded that the history leaving a restarted owner in that state was not constructed. The new harness builds it: the owner first admits a client operation for its own instance (0,0), so the instance exists with leader bookkeeping and a pending proposal (the local run shows status PREACCEPTED with one pending); the restart is then modelled by constructing a fresh replica with no durable state (no record for the instance); the recovery-led PreAccept recreates the record without bookkeeping; and the legal single-NONE Commit follows. The same nil-pointer panic results: panicked true with the dereference value and no commit effect.\\n\\nProduct. A second artifact on the same unit (unit-C4-noop-commit-without-bookkeeping) with the reviewed plan and the strengthened harness, submitted for execution by the trusted runner and a fresh correspondence review. The obligation, predicate, prerequisite condition, identity correlation and handler calls are unchanged — only the input history is now constructed rather than assumed, and the modelling choice (a fresh replica for the restart, justified by the shipped configuration's durable=false) is stated in the submission rationale.\\n\\nFrontier. The crash family now reads as: a replica that crashed and restarted, with an instance it had proposed, can be terminated by the NOOP commit a recoverer broadcasts — reproduced from a constructed history, with the process-death step still inferred from the run loop having no recover. The eleven claim families, the two paused candidates and the remaining unread items (the reader-side reaction to a displaced stream) are otherwise unchanged, and no requirement, premise or earlier observation was weakened.\"}"}}
